work/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local Claude tool permissions. Machine-specific, contains absolute paths,
# and has nothing to do with producing an episode.
.claude/
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# repo/ is a checkout of the PUBLIC feed repo. In CI it is created by a second
# actions/checkout step. Committing it here would nest one git repo inside
# another and push public episode audio into the private source repo.
repo/

# Personal episodes stay out of git entirely until the private-hosting question
# is settled. They contain family names, travel dates and payday. iCloud is
# already backing them up.
scripts-private/

# A clone of microsoft/markitdown living inside scripts/. Two hazards, which
# is why it is named explicitly rather than left to chance:
#   - 144 of its files are .txt/.md under scripts/, which is exactly the path
#     filter that triggers the publish workflow. Committing any of them starts
#     a publish run.
#   - it is ~9,400 files with its own .git/, so it would land as a stray
#     gitlink in a repo that is meant to hold a publisher and some scripts.
# Git currently declines to recurse into it because of that nested .git, which
# is the only reason `ship` has not tripped over it. Remove the nested .git and
# that protection disappears -- hence this line. Better still, move the clone
# somewhere outside scripts/.
scripts/markitdown/

# Scratch copies of real scripts, date-stamped like the real thing. Outside
# scripts/ so CI never sees them; ignored so they cannot be committed by
# accident and then picked up after someone moves one.
scripts-test/

# assets/*.wav ARE committed on purpose. audio_post.master() skips the music
# beds silently when they are missing, so a runner without them produces a
# quietly worse episode rather than an error.
